# Fixed-step steepest descent. develop reads sd_alpha from [SD]; the step is dr = sd_alpha * F, then the same per-atom cap. sd_twopoint defaults off.
# Archive config.ini sets sd_alpha 0.04 and max_move 0.2. The library default alpha is 0.1. comments.txt says 0.001; that sentence is the LJ38 comment, and the client does not read it.
# The stop is the Euclidean norm of the free forces at 0.001, which is r2030 getForcesFreeV().norm() and convergence_metric norm here. Not the max atom force.
# report.sh counts a start failed at 10000 force calls. That is the problem cap. This run allows 10000.
# HarnessCounter through ext_pot. Kernel is r2549 Morse::force. Fortran-linked develop 500350d9.
counter harness
count_keys HarnessCounter
code eOn (develop 500350d9)
code_version 3.6.0
commit 500350d9fae881f06c7ef194e5868da079c4be5a
algorithm SD
tuning archive
template eon-develop/morse-sd-stock
problem minimization/morse-bulk
reducer harness
cap 10000
n 100
par2_mean 196.4
nfailed 0
mean_calls 196.4
median_calls 180.0
force_calls 196
force_calls_min 95
force_calls_max 360
n_crash 0
n_divergence 0
n_cap 0
n_wrong_stationary 0
